y may be used only as required to load or run the checkpoint (e.g., model definition, preprocessing). Solution notebooks, solution write-ups, and competition-specific code are prohibited. - Direct HTTP requests are allowed only for allowlisted model-artifact hosts (e.g., `huggingface.co`, `download.pytorch.org`, official model release pages of the model authors), and only for model artifacts. Prefer official libraries.  2. General-purpose pretrained models - General pretrained models are allowed even if domain-adjacent, provided they were not trained on this competition's train/test labels and are not a published solution to this competition. - Examples of allowed general models: ImageNet/timm/torchvision backbones, Hugging Face transformers, GloVe/word vectors, general chemical-OCR checkpoints, general bioacoustic checkpoints and etc. - Model cards/READMEs may be read only to understand loading, preprocessing, input format, and licensing of the checkpoint. They must not be used as competition write-ups.  3. Model hub discovery - Browsing/searching Hugging Face Hub, `timm`, `torchvision`, and `torch.hub` for model checkpoints is allowed. - Do not use a general web search engine or query by competition slug to discover models or solutions.  ### Prohibited  1. Live web search - No Google, Bing, DuckDuckGo, Perplexity, or any other search engine. - No `requests.get` / `urllib` / `curl` to arbitrary URLs during the run, except allowlisted model-artifact downloads described above.  2. Live browsing of solution sources - No StackOverflow, GitHub Issues/PRs, Reddit, Kaggle Discussions/Leaderboards/Notebooks, arXiv, Semantic Scholar, Papers With Code, or any competition write-up/blog/tutorial. - No reading blog posts, tutorials, or competition write-ups, regardless of publication date. - No Kaggle competition overview/evaluation pages. Use local `TASK.md` and `data/README.md` instead.  3. External APIs for solution generation - No calling external LLM endpoints (OpenAI, Ant